    <item>
      <title>We Should Worry More About English Girls' Education</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-12/we-should-worry-more-about-english-girls-education</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a673a73e4d36cf5aa7b92ade</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:00:06 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The UK, for all its political instability and sluggish growth, recently got some good news: British students ranked in the top 10 across all tested subjects in the latest results from the OECD’s Programme for International Student Assessment (PISA). The UK was one of just eight countries to achieve that feat — 92 countries and cities participated — and also managed to buck wider downward trends by improving its average science score and avoiding a decline in reading.</description>
      <dc:creator>Lara Williams</dc:creator>
